<EncodedData EncodedType="AddOnInstructionDefinition" Name="raC_Dvc_K5100_MAS" Class="Standard" Revision="1.1" RevisionExtension=".01" Vendor="Rockwell Automation" EditedDate="2019-11-25T01:49:06.727Z" SoftwareRevision="v32.00" EncryptionConfig="9">
<Description>
<![CDATA[K5100 (2198-Exxxx-ERS) - Stop the drive.]]>
</Description>
<RevisionNote>
<![CDATA[September 2019, initial release.
December 2019, issues MAS always even if Input.Stopped is 1.]]>
</RevisionNote>
<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[============================================================
Instruction Overview:
-----
K5100 (2198-Exxxx-ERS) - Stop the drive.


Supplemental Descriptions:
-----
100 – Drive is not ready.
101 – Drive is faulted.
103 – MSF is executing.
105 – Drive is disabled.
107 – MAS is executing.
113 – DecleReference is out of range.
127 – Previous command has not completed.
129 – Motor is not connected.


Revision Notes:
-----
1.1.01
- September 2019, initial release.


=============================================================== 

